From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:33:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: h265dec: don't copy frames for right/bottom-only
 cropping

When downstream supports GstVideoMeta, a conformance window that only
crops the right and bottom edges needs no copy: the output caps already
carry the display size and the video meta carries the real strides and
plane offsets, as v4l2slh264dec does. 1080p streams are coded as 1088
lines and cropped this way, so until now every 1080p frame was copied.

The copy reads from the decoder's uncached CAPTURE buffers. On a
Rockchip RK3566 (rkvdec, mainline 6.18) a 1080p stream decoded at about
5 fps into kmssink; without the copy it is about 320 fps into
fakevideosink and display rate into kmssink.
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c
index 72ca794..7735d7f 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265dec.c
@@ -1012,7 +1012,12 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_h265_dec_new_sequence (GstH265Decoder * decoder,
       }
     }
   } else {
-    self->copy_frames = self->need_crop;
+    /* With GstVideoMeta, a crop of the right and bottom edges only needs
+     * no copy: downstream takes the display size from the caps and the
+     * buffer layout from the meta, as with v4l2slh264dec. 1080p streams
+     * are coded as 1088 lines and cropped this way. */
+    self->copy_frames = self->need_crop &&
+        (self->crop_rect_x != 0 || self->crop_rect_y != 0);
   }
 
   return GST_FLOW_OK;
